C03: an order that almost names an installed game asks whether to open it (GAMES1533)

«Ve a Mad de Rivals.» was read as going to a web site («Mad de Rivals»: a public search and a navigation to a stranger's page) when the owner meant Marvel Rivals, installed in their library. `effect_intent.near_catalog_game_candidates` reads an open, launch or go-to order whose target shares a word of five or more letters with an installed game's title (or is one or two edits away), excluding exact matches and deictics; the turn asks whether to open it with the same validated clarifier as near-miss applications (APPS1499): zero operations, no search, no launch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


